// lexdb over TNS: the third bug slice (design/lexdb-robust.md, "The third bug slice"), checked against Oracle Database Free 23.26
// (gen_oracle.py --check tns_bugs3): MIN and MAX of equal instants with different offsets keep the first one read (a keyed table
// filled in key order, a keyless one, an index on the column, GROUP BY, a window, NULLs, no rows); a TIMESTAMP WITH LOCAL TIME
// ZONE value is type 231 (in DBTIMEZONE); a datetime plus an INTERVAL YEAR TO MONTH whose day is not in the month is ORA-01839
// (DATE, TIMESTAMP, TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE moved in UTC, NUMTOYMINTERVAL; ADD_MONTHS clamps); OFFSET and LIMIT as column
// aliases, column names and a table's alias; views that call a stored function and a package's function (in the select list, in
// WHERE, with a constant argument, joined, counted, the function replaced after; USER_VIEWS.TEXT as written); a column annotation in
// CREATE TABLE AS (ORA-11559), a column twice in ALTER TABLE ... MODIFY (ORA-00957), ALTER INDEX of no index (ORA-01418), REBUILD
// and COALESCE (accepted), ALTER TABLE of a view and ALTER VIEW of a table (ORA-00942), ALTER VIEW ... COMPILE (accepted) and
// RENAME TO (ORA-00922). Each statement runs with set lexdb_batch = off (the row engine) and on: "same" and the answer, or
// DIFFERENT and both.
// expect: setup: 36 statements
// expect: same: MN,MX = '10:00 +02:00'|'10:00 +02:00'
// expect: same: G,MN,MX,N = 1|'10:00 +02:00'|'10:00 +02:00'|3;2|'07:00 +00:00'|'07:00 +00:00'|2;3|NULL|NULL|0
